---
// Privacy policy text, shown in a pop-up (see Base.astro). Update the date when the policy changes.
import { business, stores } from '../data/site.js';
const effective = 'November 5, 2026';
const mail = `mailto:${business.privacyEmail}`;
---
<article class="legal">
  <p class="legal__date">Effective {effective}</p>

  <p>Polka Deli ("we", "us") runs this website, polkadelimd.com, for our stores in Silver Spring, MD and Vienna, VA. We keep things simple: we only collect what we need to answer you, send you deli news you asked for, and (in the future) fill your orders. We never sell your information.</p>

  <h2>What we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mailing list.</strong> Your name and email address when you join our mailing list.</li>
    <li><strong>Contact form.</strong> Your name, email address and message when you write to us.</li>
    <li><strong>Online orders</strong> (when our online store opens). Your name, contact details, delivery or pickup details and order history. Payments are handled by our store provider; we never see or store your full card number.</li>
    <li><strong>Basic technical data.</strong> Like every website, our hosting provider automatically receives standard information such as your IP address and browser type so the site can load and stay secure.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To send you our newsletter: exclusive news and offers, such as specials, coupons and holiday hours. We send only a handful of emails a year.</li>
    <li>To reply to your questions and help with your orders.</li>
    <li>To process, prepare and deliver online orders, and to send receipts and order updates.</li>
    <li>To keep the website running, secure and free of spam.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who helps us</h2>
  <p>We use a few trusted services to run the site. They handle your information only to provide their service to us:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Netlify</strong> hosts this website and receives contact form messages.</li>
    <li><strong>Our email newsletter service</strong> (currently Kit) stores the mailing list and sends our emails.</li>
    <li><strong>Shopify</strong> will run our online store and payments once it opens.</li>
    <li><strong>Google</strong> provides the maps on our Visit us page and the fonts on this site, and <strong>Uber Eats</strong> handles orders placed through its app. When you use those, their own privacy policies apply.</li>
    <li><strong>Facebook and Instagram</strong> links take you to those sites, which have their own privacy policies.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We don't sell, rent or trade your personal information, and we don't share it with anyone for their own marketing.</p>

  <h2>Unsubscribing and your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every newsletter has an <strong>unsubscribe</strong> link at the bottom. One click and you're off the list.</li>
    <li>You can ask us to see, correct or delete the information we have about you at any time by emailing <a href={mail}>{business.privacyEmail}</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>We keep your email on our mailing list until you unsubscribe. We keep contact messages only as long as we need them to help you, and order records as long as required for taxes and accounting.</p>

  <h2>Keeping it safe</h2>
  <p>This site uses a secure (https) connection, and the services we use protect your data with industry-standard security. No website can be perfectly secure, but we only collect what we need, which keeps the risk small.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If we change how we handle your information, we'll update this policy and the date at the top.</p>

  <h2>Contact us</h2>
  <p>Questions about your privacy? Email <a href={mail}>{business.privacyEmail}</a>, or call us at <a href={stores[0].phoneHref}>{stores[0].phone}</a> (Silver Spring) or <a href={stores[1].phoneHref}>{stores[1].phone}</a> (Vienna).</p>
</article>
